{
  "schema": "ld-s10y-image/figure-spec@2",
  "id": "fig-48",
  "mode": "deterministic",
  "description": "fig-48: inspect the original function's increasing/decreasing behavior in its original grid and extent. Source facts are confined to source.inventory and source-inventory.json. Authored additions: Semantic ink/grid/paper roles replace scan texture, preserving mathematical solid/dashed distinctions. Margins, horizontal Arial labels, explicit source-coordinate label placement, and readable fixed-640 composition are authored layout choices. Subpixel point objects only bind assertions to the curve. No visible named points, endpoint circles, coordinate labels, or answer annotations are added. No Cyrillic/Chinese caption, equation beyond the original, explanatory text, or new numeric tick is visible. Exact plotted boundary heights [[-10,-1.3333333333333335],[14,6.666666666666667]] are calculated from the authoritative line equation at the source grid's x bounds, not invented high-precision scan readings.",
  "source": {
    "image": {
      "path": "ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/7a/figures/fig-48.png",
      "sha256": "a54c9daafa15b6c7371d1c09af93f533dd514fb4270c7653c9841c9cc6684f41"
    },
    "authoritativeText": [
      {
        "lesson": "alg7-c4-s1-n34",
        "text": "例1 在图48和49里画出了下列两个线性函数的图象：\n$y=\\frac{1}{3}x+2$ 和 $y=-0.5x+1$.*"
      },
      {
        "lesson": "alg7-c4-s1-n34",
        "text": "如果在整个定义域上函数 $f$ 总是增大（或者减小），那么就说，$f$ 是增函数（或者减函数）."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "alg7-c4-s1-n34",
        "text": "下面我们举几个我们熟悉的函数的例子，并且说明它们的变化情况."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "alg7-c4-s1-n34",
        "text": "图48"
      },
      {
        "lesson": "alg7-c4-s1-n34",
        "text": "图49"
      }
    ],
    "inventory": [
      {
        "id": "source-grid-inventory",
        "description": "12 columns and 12 rows; 13 vertical / 13 horizontal lines; bounds [-10,16,14,-8], steps 2/2, zero offsets. Uniform square cells with TWO coordinate units per cell on both axes.",
        "objects": [
          "source-grid"
        ],
        "assertions": [
          "source-grid-dimensions"
        ],
        "requires": [
          "gridDimensions"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "source-axes-inventory",
        "description": "One shared Cartesian frame, x/y labels, positive-direction arrowheads and origin 0. The grid provides the unnumbered divisions; printed numeric labels are inventoried separately.",
